# Each suppression here is a CALLER decision that the module exposes as a variable, not a
# weakness in the module. Anything that is genuinely the module's responsibility should be
# fixed rather than listed.

# CloudFront access logging is not enabled by default.
# Exposed as var.logging. Off by default because CloudFront's legacy logging_config
# requires the target bucket to have ACLs enabled with BucketOwnerPreferred, which
# conflicts with the BucketOwnerEnforced default AWS applies to new buckets — so the module
# cannot turn it on without either creating a non-conforming bucket or failing.
AVD-AWS-0010

# CloudFront distribution does not have a WAF in front of it.
# Exposed as var.web_acl_id. A WAFv2 ACL is an account-level resource with its own cost and
# rule lifecycle; creating one per static site would be wrong.
AVD-AWS-0011

# S3 bucket does not have logging enabled.
# Access logging on the origin bucket needs a caller-owned target bucket. CloudFront logs
# are the useful signal for a site served through a distribution.
AVD-AWS-0089
